// ========================================================================
// DisableAutostart.tmc — Load this program when you want a program-free board.
// Safe to run in any state: mid-move, stuck sled, CL fighting an obstacle.
//
// What it does:
//   1. Boosts deceleration for a fast controlled stop.
//   2. Stops all motors (MST).
//   3. Waits 500 ms for all axes to fully decelerate to rest.
//   4. Disables closed-loop and zeros all currents — fully de-energizes motors.
//   5. Disables auto-start (SGP 77, Bank 0 = 0) — stored in EEPROM, survives
//      power cycles. After this runs, pressing the red button or powering on
//      the board will NOT restart any program automatically.
//   6. Immediately stops.
//
// To restore normal operation:
//   Load TMCMCode_newversion.tmc via TMCL-IDE and re-enable auto-start
//   (check the "auto-start" option in the TMCL-IDE upload settings, or
//   manually set SGP 77, Bank 0 = 1 before loading).
// ========================================================================

SAP 17, 0, 1000000  // boost deceleration for fast controlled stop
SAP 17, 1, 1000000
SAP 17, 2, 1000000
MST 0               // stop all motors
MST 1
MST 2
WAIT TICKS,0,500    // wait 500 ms — enough for any axis to fully decelerate to rest
SAP 129, 0, 0       // disable closed-loop axis 0
SAP 129, 1, 0       // disable closed-loop axis 1
SAP 129, 2, 0       // disable closed-loop axis 2
SAP 6, 0, 0         // zero run current axis 0
SAP 6, 1, 0         // zero run current axis 1
SAP 6, 2, 0         // zero run current axis 2
SAP 7, 0, 0         // zero standby current axis 0
SAP 7, 1, 0         // zero standby current axis 1
SAP 7, 2, 0         // zero standby current axis 2
SGP 77, 0, 0        // disable auto-start (EEPROM Bank 0 — persists across power cycles)
STOP
